  "step_3": "The decision reason based on skewness would favor a lottery with more probability mass on favorable (less negative) outcomes. In this case, both lotteries have 75% of probability on outcomes ≥ -2000, but B has 75% on 0, while A has only 50% on 0. Thus, B is more concentrated on the best outcome, which aligns with being more left-skewed. The individual’s reasoning focuses on the higher chance of no loss in B (75% vs 50%), which corresponds to the same feature — concentration of probability on the best outcome. While the individual does not mention 'skewness' explicitly, their focus on the higher probability of avoiding losses entirely aligns with the informational basis of the skewness reason. The justification (preferring higher probability of no loss) is consistent with preferring a more left-skewed distribution. Therefore, the information considered and the justification are closely aligned with the skewness reason, even if not named as such.",
